[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ACE-Project-Team/theprovingground/main/media/header.gif[/img]

[h1]The Proving Ground[/h1]
A team gamemode for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3333669763]Armored Combat Extended[/url], heavily inspired by the Baiknor combined arms gamemode. Green against Red: build your vehicle in spawn, drive it out, and fight for the map alongside the infantry.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ACE-Project-Team/theprovingground/main/media/gameplay.gif[/img]

[h2]How a round works[/h2]
[list]
[*]Both teams start with a pool of tickets. Whatever the mode, you win by draining the other team's pool to zero.
[*]Each round opens with a short prep window. Teams are held in spawn while they build.
[*]Every team has a point budget for its vehicles, set per map and priced with ACE's own point values.
[*]The team that's behind gets some help, so a lost start doesn't decide the round.
[/list]

[h2]Game modes[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ACE-Project-Team/theprovingground/main/media/modes.gif[/img]

One is picked at random each round:
[list]
[*][b]Control Points[/b] - capture and hold points around the map.
[*][b]King of the Hill[/b] - hold the central point.
[*][b]Rush[/b] - one point at a time; take it and hold it.
[*][b]Capture the Flag[/b] - one neutral flag on the hill; carry it to your own spawn to score.
[*][b]Deathmatch[/b] - destroy enemy vehicles.
[/list]

[h2]Your soldier[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ACE-Project-Team/theprovingground/main/media/loadout.gif[/img]

[h2]Also in[/h2]
[list]
[*]Loadouts: armour tiers from None to Juggernaut, plus primary, secondary and special weapons.
[*]Stats, rating and ranks, from Traffic Cone upwards, plus end-of-round commendations. They are saved on the server; a global leaderboard is on the way - check out [url=https://acegmod.com]acegmod.com[/url].
[*]Rock the vote, team scramble votes and an end-of-map map vote.
[*]A per-player economy (beta): some rounds give each player their own wallet in place of the shared team budget.
[*]Q-menu settings for players and admins: team, menus and HUD toggles for everyone, and round, map editor and server settings for admins.
[/list]

[h2]NPC bots (partial support)[/h2]
Servers can fill out thin teams with NPC soldiers, with [b]tpg_bots_fill[/b] set to the team size wanted. Support is partial and still being worked on, so expect rough edges. Bots:
[list]
[*]capture and hold points, keeping part of the team in cover around a taken point while the rest pushes on;
[*]take the enemy flag in CTF and run it home, shooting on the way (with Combat AI);
[*]carry ACE weapons, and a share of them carry AT4s for enemy armour;
[*]run from live grenades, and react to ACE gunfire and explosions;
[*]ride in vehicle seats their owner marks with the TPG E2 & Starfall functions, getting out at the exit point the owner sets. Riders show in the seat and get hurt when it is hit.
[/list]
They work on their own, and fight better with the Combat AI addon installed. They only spawn on maps with an AI node graph, or a Combat AI navmesh. Bots don't drive vehicles yet.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3333669763]Armored Combat Extended[/url]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3154971187]Contraption Framework[/url]. Without it, TPG falls back to weight-based limits.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3820591473]TPG E2 & Starfall Team Functions[/url], for servers. TPG has no chip functions of its own.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=159298542]Nadmod Prop Protection[/url]. Without prop protection, vehicles are not protected in the safezones.
[/list]
On startup the server prints a warning to its console if any of these are missing.

[h2]Running a server[/h2]
Subscribe the server to this item and the ones above, then start it with [b]+gamemode theprovingground[/b]. 27 maps come with spawns, budgets and objectives set up, among them gm_construct, gm_flatgrass, gm_diprip_refinery and the gm_baik and gm_emp series. On any other map, admins can lay it out in game with the TPG Point Tool and the map editor ([b]tpg_mapedit[/b]): spawns, objectives, the CTF flag, budgets and capture speeds.

